  "title": "SINGSING",
  "description": "This dataset contains simultaneous EEG and MEG recordings from twenty adult participants presented with harmonic complex sound (HCS) stimuli varying in frequency, in an auditory oddball paradigm. The study investigates pre-attentive pitch processing at both sensor and source levels, comparing EEG and MEG responses. Data acquisition was conducted at the MEG Centre, Timone Hospital, Marseille, France.",
  "methods_description": "Twenty adult participants were presented with harmonic complex sound stimuli varying in frequency in an auditory oddball protocol, during simultaneous EEG and MEG recording.",
